      [1;32m# [0m[1;32mTerminal-wrapped links[0m

      Render this document
      with OSC8 off and a zero
      right margin to check
      contiguous URL bytes and
      natural terminal
      wrapping. Words after
      each URL should resume
      at the correct column,
      then wrap normally with
      the configured left
      margin.

      Click detection also
      depends on the terminal
      and multiplexer. For
      tmux, use OSC8 on with a
      supporting terminal and
      tmux's hyperlinks
      feature enabled. The
      no-OSC8 goldens verify
      URL bytes and layout;
      mouse-click handling
      belongs to the terminal
      and multiplexer.

      The example.com
      addresses below are
      rendering examples, not
      live documentation
      pages.

      [1;34m## [0m[1;34mParagraph[0m

      Read the [4m[1;34mlong report[0m
      ([90mhttps://example.com/documentation/terminal-wrapping/long-link-demonstration/keeping-the-entire-destination-clickable?session=0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef&source=golden[0m)
      and then keep reading
      this sentence. These
      words should fill the
      space left on the
      terminal row before the
      next ordinary line
      break.

